#
# OntoUML metamodel model — the MixRig anti-pattern (documented in the OntoUML
# anti-pattern catalogue at https://ontouml.readthedocs.io/en/latest/anti-patterns/).
#
# A rigid sortal (kind/subkind) must never specialize an anti-rigid type (role,
# phase, mixin, …): a rigid type cannot inherit contingent instantiation.
# ex:SpecialCitizen is a rigid subkind whose ancestor ex:Voter is an anti-rigid
# role, so it violates the discipline. The documented verdict is MixRig.

@prefix ontouml: <https://w3id.org/ontouml#> .
@prefix ex:      <https://gmeow.example/ontouml-mini/mix-rig/> .

ex:Voter          a ontouml:Class ; ontouml:stereotype ontouml:role .
ex:SpecialCitizen a ontouml:Class ; ontouml:stereotype ontouml:subkind .

ex:g1 a ontouml:Generalization ;
    ontouml:general  ex:Voter ;
    ontouml:specific ex:SpecialCitizen .
